  "dependencies": [
    "WP-002"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "`GET /api/models` returns the model array, auto-initializing `local.json` from defaults on first access",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/models` auto-generates UUIDv4 for entries without `id` and persists all entries",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/models` with a duplicate slug returns a validation error",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/models` with reserved slug `\"inherit\"` on a non-sentinel entry returns a validation error",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/models` removing a referenced model returns 409 Conflict with a list of usages directing the user to the Replace Model feature",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/models` removing an unreferenced model succeeds",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/models/load-defaults` merges defaults without overwriting existing entries and returns slug-collision conflicts",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`GET /api/model-assignments` returns assignments enriched with `stale: true` when `max(mtime(assignments.json), mtime(local.json))` > `mtime(name-mapping.json)`, `stale: false` when neither user file exists, and `stale: false` when only `default.json` is newer",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`PUT /api/model-assignments` validates model UUIDs exist in registry and persona keys exist in `name-mapping.json`; returns 400 when `name-mapping.json` doesn't exist",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/model-assignments/replace` swaps all occurrences of `old_model_id` with `new_model_id`; rejects when `old_model_id` is not referenced (400); rejects when `old_model_id === new_model_id` (400 \"Source and target models must be different\")",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`GET /api/personas` returns all personas from `name-mapping.json` when it exists, or empty array when it doesn't",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/personas/rebuild` spawns `node scripts/build-personas.js`, returns `{ success: true, output }` on exit 0 and `{ success: false, output, exitCode }` with HTTP 500 on failure",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "`POST /api/personas/rebuild` returns 409 when a build is already in progress; clears the `buildInProgress` flag on process errors (finally-block cleanup)",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "All 8 API client methods are added and call the correct endpoints with correct HTTP methods",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "All integration tests pass",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "security-audit",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T14:41:46Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T14:49:42Z",
      "duration_ms": 476000,
      "summary": [
        "Created mcp-server/gui/api-models.ts with all 8 handler functions: handleGetModels, handleSaveModels, handleLoadDefaults, handleGetAssignments, handleUpdateAssignments, handleReplaceAssignedModel, handleGetPersonas, handleRebuildPersonas.",
        "handleSaveModels: auto-assigns UUIDv4 via randomUUID() for entries missing id; delegates to writeModels() which enforces slug uniqueness, reserved-slug guard, and deletion guard; returns 409 CONFLICT with referencedModels details when a deletion is blocked.",
        "handleGetAssignments: computes stale boolean by comparing max(mtime(assignments.json), mtime(local.json)) against mtime(name-mapping.json); default.json excluded from comparison; returns stale:false when neither user file exists.",
        "handleUpdateAssignments: validates name-mapping.json existence (400 if absent); validates all persona keys against id values in name-mapping.json; validates all model UUIDs against registry.",
        "handleReplaceAssignedModel: rejects same-model swap with message 'Source and target models must be different'; rejects when old_model_id not referenced; swaps all occurrences including default_model_uuid.",
        "handleGetPersonas: reads name-mapping.json, returns empty array on ENOENT.",
        "handleRebuildPersonas: module-level buildInProgress concurrency guard (409 on concurrent); spawns node scripts/build-personas.js non-detached; captures stdout+stderr; clears flag in finally block.",
        "Registered 3 GET routes in matchRoute() (models, model-assignments, personas) and 5 body-parsing routes in handleRequest() (PUT models, POST models/load-defaults, PUT model-assignments, POST model-assignments/replace, POST personas/rebuild).",
        "Added 8 API client methods to api-client.js: getModels, saveModels, loadDefaultModels, getPersonas, getAssignments, updateAssignments, replaceAssignedModel, rebuildPersonas.",
        "Created 36-test integration test file covering all 13 acceptance criteria scenarios.",
        "All 3523 tests pass across 117 test files. TypeScript compilation clean (0 errors)."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/gui/api-models.ts",
          "mcp-server/gui/server.ts",
          "mcp-server/gui/public/api-client.js",
          "mcp-server/tests/gui/api-models.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:49:42Z",
          "note": "server.ts handleRequest() has grown substantially (~1900 lines) and now handles 5 more body-parsing routes inline. The inline body-parsing pattern (repeated try/catch/sendError boilerplate for each route) is functional but verbose. A future refactor could introduce a typed route registry or a dispatchBodyRoute() helper to reduce duplication. Out of scope for this WP but worth noting for maintainability."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:49:42Z",
          "note": "api-models.ts handleRebuildPersonas() uses a non-typed Promise wrapper around spawn() events. The pattern is correct and mirrors orchestrator-manager.ts, but a typed utility wrapper (e.g. spawnWithOutput(cmd, args, cwd): Promise<{output, exitCode}>) shared between the two callers would eliminate duplication if a third caller appears."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:49:42Z",
          "note": "handleUpdateAssignments() reads both name-mapping.json and local.json in sequence. Both reads are independent and could be parallelized with Promise.all() to reduce latency for users with large registries. Minor optimization opportunity."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:49:42Z",
          "note": "The _resetBuildInProgress() export in api-models.ts uses an underscore prefix to signal 'test-only'. The project doesn't have an established convention for this (api-repos.ts has no test-only exports). A JSDoc @internal tag is present which is sufficient; just noting the minor convention gap."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T14:55:05Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T14:58:39Z",
      "duration_ms": 214000,
      "summary": [
        "TypeScript compilation: 0 errors (npx tsc --noEmit clean).",
        "Integration tests: all 36 tests in api-models.test.ts pass — covering all 15 ACs (AC-1 through AC-13 handler tests, AC-14 API client methods verified by code inspection, AC-15 test suite pass).",
        "Full regression: 3523 tests across 117 test files — all pass, no regressions.",
        "Edge-case analysis: 10 targeted checks passed — strict '>' stale comparison (equal mtimes → not stale), optional default_model_uuid skipped in validation when undefined, ReplaceModelBodySchema uses .strict() to reject extra fields, SaveModelsBodySchema defaults cc_model to 'inherit', finally-block clears buildInProgress on process error, ApiError re-export present for consumer use, handleGetPersonas rejects non-array name-mapping.json.",
        "Route registration: all 3 GET routes in matchRoute() and all 5 body-parsing POST/PUT routes in handleRequest() confirmed correct. CONFLICT→409 and VALIDATION_ERROR→400 HTTP mappings verified.",
        "POST /api/personas/rebuild server handler correctly returns HTTP 500 for { success: false } without throwing (uses result.success ? 200 : 500 pattern)."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "36/36 integration tests, 117 test files total",
        "tests_passed": 3523,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:58:39Z",
          "note": "The 8 new API client methods in api-client.js (getModels, saveModels, loadDefaultModels, getPersonas, getAssignments, updateAssignments, replaceAssignedModel, rebuildPersonas) are not covered by the existing api-client.test.ts test file. AC-14 is met (methods exist and call correct endpoints), but unit test coverage for these methods would improve confidence in future refactors. Consider adding client-side unit tests in a follow-up."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:58:39Z",
          "note": "computeStale uses strict '>' for the freshness comparison — equal mtimes return stale: false, which is the correct spec behavior. No test directly asserts this boundary (equal mtime → not stale), though the three existing stale-detection tests adequately cover the specified scenarios. A boundary test would make the invariant explicit."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T14:58:39Z",
          "note": "No improvement — code is clean, patterns are consistent, and all acceptance criteria are fully verified."
        }
      ]
