      "type": "security-audit",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T14:59:04Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T15:00:49Z",
      "duration_ms": 105000,
      "summary": [
        "Reviewed 4 files (api-models.ts, server.ts, src/gui/model-registry.ts, gui/public/api-client.js). 0 Critical, 0 High, 1 Medium (info disclosure in validation error — noted), 1 Info (unconstrained cast in handleGetPersonas). Security sign-off: PASS."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "security_issues": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:00:49Z",
          "note": "Medium — A05 (Security Misconfiguration / Information Disclosure). File: mcp-server/gui/api-models.ts, line ~339 (handleUpdateAssignments). The validation error message for an invalid persona key leaks the full list of valid persona IDs: `Valid IDs are: ${[...validPersonaIds].join(', ')}`. In this context the risk is low (GUI is localhost-bound, CORS is restricted, persona IDs are not secrets), but this is an unnecessary detail in an error message. Remediation: emit only the count of valid IDs or a generic message (e.g. 'Persona key X does not exist in name-mapping.json. Run a build to refresh the persona list.') rather than enumerating all valid values."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:00:49Z",
          "note": "Info — A04 (Insecure Design / Type Safety). File: mcp-server/gui/api-models.ts, line ~507 (handleGetPersonas). The final return statement `return parsed as PersonaEntry[]` casts the JSON-parsed array to the PersonaEntry interface without Zod validation of individual entry shapes. The file is locally owned (not user-submitted) so direct exploitation risk is minimal. If this data ever feeds server-side logic beyond display, a Zod schema parse should be added. For the current read-only display use case this is informational only."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T15:00:49Z",
          "note": "No security findings in the following areas — all OWASP Top 10 categories reviewed: A01 (path construction uses hardcoded WORKSPACE_ROOT, not user input), A02 (no secrets or sensitive data stored; randomUUID() from Node crypto), A03 (all inputs validated via Zod before use; spawn uses a hardcoded script path with no user-controlled arguments), A06 (no new third-party dependencies introduced), A07 (no auth endpoints; not applicable to this local GUI server), A08 (no deserialization of untrusted data; atomic writes used), A09 (errors logged to stderr only, no stack traces returned to callers), A10 (no server-side URL fetching). CORS restricted to localhost. Security headers applied on all responses (CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy). Body size capped at 1 MiB. UUID fields validated with z.string().uuid() and existence-checked against live registry."
        }
      ]
    }
